---
import './misses.css';
import { admissionTrace } from './model.mjs';
const initial = admissionTrace()[0];
---
<figure class="miss-figure" data-miss-admission>
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 5</span>Different keys, one source budget</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="controls"><label>Source read <select data-duration><option value="100">100 ms</option><option value="200">200 ms</option></select></label></div>
  <div class="label" data-clock data-live>Clock 0 ms · caller deadline 150 ms</div>
  <div class="counters" data-live><div><strong data-started>0</strong><span>Source reads started</span></div><div><strong data-active>0</strong><span>Source slots occupied</span></div><div><strong data-answered>0</strong><span>On-time answers</span></div><div><strong data-failed>0</strong><span>Callers rejected or timed out</span></div></div>
  <div class="admission-board">
   <div class="zone zone-source"><span class="label">Source · 2 slots</span></div>
   <div class="zone zone-queue"><span class="label">Queue · 2 places</span></div>
   <div class="zone zone-outcomes"><span class="label">Arrivals and outcomes</span></div>
   {initial.jobs.map((job,i) => <div class="moving-token" data-job={job.key} data-live style={`left:${i % 2 ? 55 : 3}%;top:${12.7 + Math.floor(i / 2) * 4}rem`}><strong>{job.key}</strong><span>{job.state}</span></div>)}
  </div>
  <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{initial.explanation}</p>
 </div>
 <div class="controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div><span data-step>1 / 9</span></div>
 <figcaption>Six invented misses arrive together in the order P7–P12. They share the north, en-GB, GBP context, but need different answers. The model knows each read’s fixed duration; a real service has variable durations. No retries or useful old copies are available. Watch a token move only when its work changes place.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>The queue trace, as text</summary><p>P7 and P8 start. P9 and P10 queue. P11 and P12 are rejected. With 100 ms reads, P7 and P8 answer at 100 ms; the queued requests have only 50 ms left, too little for another 100 ms read, so they are rejected. With 200 ms reads, all remaining callers reach their 150 ms deadline first. Queued work is removed, but the two running reads retain their slots until completion at 200 ms. The slow run produces zero on-time answers from two source reads.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import { stepper } from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 import { admissionTrace } from './model.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-miss-admission]').forEach(root => {
  const duration = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-duration]')!;
  let trace = admissionTrace();
  const text = (selector: string, value: string | number) => { root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent = String(value); };
  const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => trace.length, draw: (step: number) => {
   const state = trace[step];
   text('[data-clock]', `Clock ${state.time} ms · caller deadline 150 ms`);
   for (const name of ['started','active','answered']) text(`[data-${name}]`, state[name]);
   const timedOut = state.time >= 150 ? state.jobs.filter(j => j.state === 'Running' || j.state === 'Late completion').length : 0;
   text('[data-failed]', state.rejected + timedOut);
   let running = 0, queued = 0;
   state.jobs.forEach((job,i) => {
    const token = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-job="${job.key}"]`)!;
    let top = 12.7 + Math.floor(i / 2) * 4, left = i % 2 ? 55 : 3;
    if (job.state === 'Running') { top = 2 + running++ * 4; left = 3; }
    if (job.state === 'Queued') { top = 2 + queued++ * 4; left = 55; }
    token.style.top = `${top}rem`; token.style.left = `${left}%`; token.dataset.state = job.state;
    token.querySelector('span')!.textContent = job.state === 'Running' && state.time >= 150 ? 'Caller left; read runs' : job.state;
   });
   text('[data-explanation]', state.explanation);
  }});
  duration.addEventListener('change', () => {
   trace = admissionTrace({ duration: Number(duration.value) });
   root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click(); player.render();
  });
 });
</script>
